For an inverse variation  
\[
y = \frac{k}{\sqrt{x}}
\]
the constant \(k\) is obtained by multiplying the given \(y\) by \(\sqrt{x}\).

\[
k = y \,\sqrt{x}
\]

With \(x = 24\) and \(y = 15\):

\[
k = 15 \times \sqrt{24}
      = 15 \times \sqrt{4 \times 6}
      = 15 \times 2 \sqrt{6}
      = 30 \sqrt{6}
\]

\[
\boxed{k = 30\sqrt{6}\;\;(\text{approximately } 73.5)}
\]
